Endofunctors and isomorphisms on the bespoke category of domains (Def 6.3 library).

**Definition (`Endofunctor`).** An endofunctor assigns to each object an object and to each morphism a morphism, such that identities and compositions are preserved.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎

**Definition (`Iso`).** An isomorphism consists of mutually inverse morphisms between two objects.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎
